<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
          xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools">
  <!--
    Release-only manifest overrides. AGP merges this on top of src/main for the
    release variant only, so debug builds (expo run:android, the EAS
    "development" profile) are untouched and the dev menu's QR scanner keeps
    working there.

    expo-dev-client is linked into every Android variant: unlike Apple, where
    expo-module.config.json's "debugOnly" flag is honored, expo-modules-autolinking
    has no Android equivalent (ExpoModuleConfig.appleDebugOnly() is read only by
    platforms/apple/apple.js). expo-dev-launcher then pulls in
    play-services-code-scanner and mlkit:barcode-scanning (its android/build.gradle
    lines 111-112) for the "scan QR to open" screen, and that AAR contributes a
    hard-coded portrait GmsBarcodeScanningDelegateActivity, which Play flagged as
    an orientation restriction on versionCode 14.

    Dropping the modules via expoAutolinking.exclude in settings.gradle does not
    work. expo-dev-client's android/build.gradle:43 declares
    androidTestImplementation project(":expo-dev-launcher"), so dev-launcher cannot
    be excluded on its own, and a multi-package exclude silently no-ops because
    AutolinkigCommandBuilder space-joins the list into one argv entry while the
    autolinking CLI expects a variadic list of separate entries.

    Removing the activity here also un-roots ML Kit for R8: the merged manifest is
    what kept roughly 326 mlkit references reachable in classes2.dex.
  -->
  <application>
    <activity
      android:name="com.google.mlkit.vision.codescanner.internal.GmsBarcodeScanningDelegateActivity"
      tools:node="remove" />
  </application>
</manifest>
